Z||000006||StuGood||11-11-2001||03:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ferrari_cdn:<BR><B>...Those drivers should be shot!...He could have crashed either that other car or wrecked my car...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>What you describe, I call "doing the weave."  Hopefully, attrition takes care of people like that.  Or better yet, they pretty soon smarten up and learn to be more thoughtful of others.  <P>One good thing about the situation you describe is, if an accident <B>did</B> occur, the driver of the other car was around to get help if necessary, and could act as a witness, too, if it came to that.<P>Anyway, like they say, courtesy really <B>is</B> contagious.  I just wish disrespect wasn't so quick to rub off.  I love it when people in traffic cooperate - it spreads like wildfire!  Pretty amazing how quickly irritated drivers can cool off, when you show them a little kindness!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>What BlackStang95 says is true, too.  But, since Fieros seem to disappear in the blind spots more than other cars, it's a good idea to leave lotsa room, of course  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.||||reg||1
